# heighttocaustics

- Label: Height to Caustics
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 47 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttocaustics.html
- Summary (EN): Treats a height layer as a refractive surface and generates caustic light patterns on the ground by tracing light through the surface, bending rays with the surface normal and accumulating where they land.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme un champ de hauteur en surface réfractive et génère les motifs de caustiques projetés au sol par traçage de photons.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the refractive surface (required)", "ground: optional height layer for the ground; if unconnected a flat plane at Ground Offset is used"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "set to RGB to enable dispersion"}, {"name": "Directional, Light Azimuth, Light Altitude, Light Position", "meaning": "control the light source"}, {"name": "Index of Refraction", "meaning": "defaults to 1.33, approximating water"}, {"name": "Ground Offset / Ground Scale", "meaning": "flat ground height, or scale of the ground input"}, {"name": "Photon Iterations / Denoise Iterations", "meaning": "trade quality and noise against cook time"}, {"name": "Method", "meaning": "Perturbation is fast but approximate; Spectrum is more accurate but expensive"}]

- Caveats: ["Dispersion parameters only apply when Signature is RGB.", "Photon Jitter Radius has no effect when Photon Iterations is 1."]

